  "level": 0,
  "ordinal": 0,
  "summary": "Gyrating Bunker Prices\nBunker prices are an important part of overall costs for operating a tanker. A Vlcc consuming 90 tons per day and sailing for, say, 320 days per year will consume 28,800 tons of bunkers. At $175 per ton, the average price of bunkers for 2004 in leading bunkering ports, the annual bunker cost is $5 million per year or $14,400 per day for a 350 day operating year including days in port.",
